<VI _name="lvbd_bind_control_refs.vi" description="Helper of lvai_bind_control_references. Turns each STAND-IN refnum control of a VI into a BOUND control reference of a real front-panel control - the node LabVIEW creates for right-click, Create, Reference - which AIXML cannot author.\0A\0ACREATE CONTROL REF ANSWERS ERROR 53 ON A WEB BROWSER CONTROL WHOSE FRONT PANEL IS CLOSED - measured 2026-10-02, the same cause as Execute JavaScript - so the panel is opened in the IDE instance first and put back to the state it was found in at the end - EVEN WHEN a step failed, which is why that write takes the read's own error and is merged afterwards. AND THE BROWSER NEEDS A MOMENT AFTER FP.Open\3A in a freshly started LabVIEW the first Create Control Ref still answered 53 and a second call a minute later succeeded, measured 2026-10-02, so a 53 is retried every 250 ms up to 40 times.\0A\0AFor each pair named in Bound Labels and Stand-In Labels it invokes {LV.Control} Create Control Ref on the bound control, reads the stand-in terminal's position, diagram and wire ends, moves the new reference node onto that diagram and position, deletes the stand-in control, and connects the new node's output to every sink the stand-in fed. It then removes the loose wire ends the delete leaves and saves the VI in place.\0A\0AWHY THE NODE IS MOVED TWICE\3A Position reads in pane coordinates while Move takes a position relative to the OWNER diagram, so the first Move reveals the offset and the second applies target + target - landed. Same as lvbd_graft_rewire.\0A\0ACONTROLS ARE FOUND BY LABEL, and their references are read once before the loop, so a deletion cannot shift a later lookup. Auto Route? is wired TRUE, because at its FALSE default LabVIEW registers the wire and draws nothing.\0A\0AOpened in the IDE application instance through Application\3AProject\3AActive Project.">
